      "description": "### Summary\r\n\r\nPostgrex does not sanitize the `:comment` query option on its streaming path. An attacker who can influence that value closes the comment delimiter with `*/` and appends clauses to the streamed statement, which execute under the connection's role. `Ecto.Repo.stream/2` forwards the same option.\r\n\r\n### Details\r\n\r\n`Postgrex.stream/4` in `lib/postgrex.ex` does not validate the `:comment` option.\r\n\r\n`parse_describe_comment_msgs/3` in `lib/postgrex/protocol.ex` concatenates the query text, `/*`, the comment, and `*/` into the statement sent in an extended-protocol `Parse` message. A comment cannot be parameterised, so the value is interpolated without escaping.\r\n\r\n`Parse` accepts one command, so a second statement cannot be chained. The streamed statement can be extended with set operations.\r\n\r\nBoth ways of consuming the stream carry the option: enumeration, and `Enum.into/2` for `COPY ... FROM STDIN`. `COPY` takes no trailing clause that composes the way `SELECT` does, so the write direction is the more restricted case.\r\n\r\n### PoC\r\n\r\n1. Create a table the application streams from, and a second table the role can read but the query does not select.\r\n2. Inside a transaction, call `Postgrex.stream/4` with a `SELECT` against the first table and `:comment` set to `*/ UNION SELECT secret FROM app_secrets --`.\r\n3. Enumerate the stream. The results include rows from the second table.\r\n4. The same comment passed to `Postgrex.query/4` raises a `Postgrex.Error`.\r\n\r\n### Impact\r\n\r\nAn attacker controlling `:comment` can read tables the database role can access, and can change state through volatile functions invoked inside the injected set operation. Applications are affected where the comment carries request, tenant, or user-supplied metadata.\r\n\r\n### References\r\n\r\n* Introducing commit: https://github.com/elixir-ecto/postgrex/commit/4971a2722fa72f8e1b54a2c403cad4c43916e36d\r\n* Patch commit: https://github.com/elixir-ecto/postgrex/commit/e1ecba618ddea4cee2556bd6ad9b6285e05f9d3c",
